Z||000000||Shianne||07-10-2001||11:29 PM||||I have an 84 2m4 with 4 speed.  I was driving along, but when I went to shift into 4th the pedal went to the floor then Became rock solid for the next shift.  The plunger seems to be moving in the slave unit.  So I am assuming something must have come apart in the bell housing.  Any Ideas.<P>Pat<BR>pneumann@telusplanet.net||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||07-11-2001||12:23 PM||||Is the clutch-fork-operating shaft actually turning when the clutch pedal is pressed?  Get a helper to press the clutch pedal while you watch the lever+ shaft.  That can be done without any disassembly.<P>I know very little about the 1984 models, but seem to remember that some of the cars (I forget which year(s)) had a nylon block in the (external) clutch operating lever - and apparently the slave cylinder's actuating rod has been known to punch a hole through the nylon block.  Another possibility is that the lever is rotating but the shaft is not -?      <P>These are hopeful suggestions; maybe they will be helpful ones, also.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000002||Shianne||07-11-2001||07:10 PM||||Well I took another look.  The arm on the transmission will move, but I think that some how the fork has slipped off of the bearing as the arm moves towards the driverside rear wheel.  I would assume under normal conditions it should move towards the engine side.  <P>I checked the arm where the slave meets the arm.  All is ok.  Any other Ideas.  I really don't want to pull the tranny, as it has only been two weeks since I got the new motor put in.  At that time every thing worked great.  I have been driving it and all seemed well.<P>Thanks<P>PAt||||reg||1
